    id: "rc-size",
    name: "Size",
    section: "S",
    ruleset: "core",
    summary:
      "The nine size categories, from smallest to largest, are Fine, Diminutive, Tiny, Small, Medium, Large, Huge, Gargantuan, and Colossal. A creature's size provides a modifier to its Armor Class and attack bonus, on grapple checks, on Hide checks, and a modifier to break open doors; size also determines how much space a creature takes up, how far it can reach, and how much it can carry. The table values (AC/attack modifier; grapple/break modifier; Hide modifier; carrying capacity multiplier; dimension — a biped's height or a quadruped's body length, nose to base of tail; approximate weight; space; reach for a tall creature; reach for a long creature): Fine — +8; -16; +16; x1/8; 6 inches or less; 1/8 lb. or less; 1/2 foot (1/100 of a square); reach 0 feet; no long reach listed. Diminutive — +4; -12; +12; x1/4; up to 1 foot; up to 1 lb.; 1 foot (1/25 square); 0 feet. Tiny — +2; -8; +8; x1/2; up to 2 feet; up to 8 lb.; 2-1/2 feet (1/4 square); 0 feet. Small — +1; -4; +4; x3/4; up to 4 feet; up to 60 lb.; 5 feet (1 square); reach 5 feet (1 square); no separate long reach. Medium — +0; +0; +0; x1; up to 8 feet; up to 500 lb.; 5 feet (1 square); reach 5 feet tall and 5 feet long. Large — -1; +4; -4; x2; up to 16 feet; up to 2 tons; 10 feet (2x2 squares); reach 10 feet tall, 5 feet long. Huge — -2; +8; -8; x4; up to 32 feet; up to 16 tons; 15 feet (3x3); reach 15 feet tall, 10 feet long. Gargantuan — -4; +12; -12; x8; up to 64 feet; up to 125 tons; 20 feet (4x4); reach 20 feet tall, 15 feet long. Colossal — -8; +16; -16; x16; 64 feet or more; 125 tons or more; 30 feet or more (6x6 or more); reach 30 feet or more tall, 20 feet or more long. (The weights assume the creature is roughly as dense as a regular animal.) Size and combat: creatures smaller than Small or larger than Medium have special rules relating to position. Little creatures: Tiny, Diminutive, and Fine creatures take up less than 1 square of space apiece — twenty-five Diminutive creatures or one hundred Fine creatures can fit into a single 5-foot square, and a Tiny creature occupies a space 2-1/2 feet across, so four can fit into a single square. Creatures that take up less than 1 square typically have a natural reach of 0 feet — they cannot reach into adjacent squares and must enter an opponent's square to attack in melee, which provokes an attack of opportunity from the opponent; you can attack into your own square, so you can attack such creatures normally; since they have no natural reach they do not threaten the squares around them, you can move past them without provoking attacks of opportunity, and they cannot flank an enemy; a creature with a reach of 0 feet still threatens the square it is in. Big creatures: Large, Huge, Gargantuan, and Colossal creatures take up more than 1 square and typically have a natural reach of 10 feet or more, so they can reach targets that are not in adjacent squares. A creature with more than 5 feet of natural reach threatens squares adjacent to it and all others within its reach, and such a creature usually gets an attack of opportunity against a Medium or smaller creature that approaches it, because that creature must enter and leave threatened squares to draw near. Large or larger creatures using reach weapons can attack at up to double their natural reach, but cannot attack within their natural reach or less.",
