      "A splash weapon is a ranged weapon that breaks on impact, splashing or scattering its contents over its target and nearby creatures or objects. When you attack with a splash weapon, you make a ranged touch attack against the target square (or a creature, if you target one). Direct hit: a successful attack deals direct hit damage to the target creature; all creatures within 5 feet of the target take splash damage (usually a fixed number). Missing: if you miss the target (whether aiming at a creature or a grid intersection), roll 1d8 to determine the direction of the deviation — counting clockwise starting from the direction from you to the target, the weapon lands in that direction at a distance equal to the range increment multiplied by the number of range increments the attack was; all creatures in that square and within 5 feet of it take splash damage; if the weapon misses a grid intersection, creatures in the square where it lands and within 5 feet take splash damage. Splash damage: creatures taking splash damage can make Reflex saves for half damage if the weapon's description allows it; the save DC is usually 15, or as given in the weapon's description. Attacking a grid intersection: to attack a specific grid intersection (AC 5), you target that intersection instead of a creature; if you hit, the weapon splashes as if it hit a creature in that square; creatures in the target square take direct hit damage if applicable. Range and thrown weapons: a splash weapon is a thrown weapon with a range increment of 10 feet unless otherwise specified; throwing a splash weapon is a standard action; preparing a splash weapon (such as filling a flask) is a full-round action.",
