    summary:
      "You can try to trip an opponent as an unarmed melee attack. You can attempt to trip your opponent in place of a melee attack. You can make only one trip attempt per round. You can trip an opponent who is one size category larger than you, the same size, or smaller — a creature cannot be tripped if it is two or more size categories larger than the tripper, or if it is formless or the DM determines it cannot be tripped. Initiating: make an unarmed melee touch attack against your target; this provokes an attack of opportunity from your target if you do not have the Improved Trip feat; if your attack succeeds, make a Strength check opposed by the defender's Dexterity or Strength check — whichever modifier is higher; a combatant gets a +4 bonus for every size category he is larger than Medium, or a -4 penalty for every size category he is smaller than Medium; the defender gets a +4 bonus on his check if he has more than two legs or is otherwise more stable than a normal humanoid. Resolving: if you win the opposed check, you trip the defender, who falls prone in his space; if you lose the opposed check, the defender may immediately make a Strength check opposed by your Dexterity or Strength check to try to trip you in return (using the same size and stability modifiers); if this counter-trip attempt fails, the defender does not get another chance to trip you. Tripping with a weapon: some weapons can be used to make trip attacks; in this case, you make a melee touch attack with the weapon instead of an unarmed melee touch attack, and you do not provoke an attack of opportunity; if you are tripped during your own trip attempt, you can drop the weapon to avoid being tripped. Tripping a mounted defender: you can make a trip attack against a mounted defender; the defender may use his Ride skill in place of his Dexterity or Strength check; if you succeed, you pull the defender off his mount and onto the ground in the defender's space. Being tripped: a tripped character is prone; standing up from prone requires a move action that provokes attacks of opportunity.",
